WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.268
You guys, last night we had
our big show in Puerto Rico.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:06.339
And I'm happy to report the
island is open for business,

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:10.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
while our government
still is not.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's right.
The federal government

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:14.614
has been closed for 26 days,
and experts say the shutdown

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:17.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
could cause the economy
to shrink.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:18.218 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Then the President said,

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:21.888
"No, it's only shrinking
'cause it's cold outside."

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:23.323 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:26.092
Well, today,
House Speaker Nancy Pelosi said

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
that due to the shutdown,
Trump should postpone

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:32.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
his State of the Union address
or do it in writing.

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which explains why Trump
just asked Twitter

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:38.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
to raise the character limit
to 50,000 words.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:41.241 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:43.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of people are calling
Pelosi's decision

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:45.245 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
a real power move.

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.379 line:92%
Even Vladimir Putin was like,

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:49.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Damn. She is not here
to make friends."

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.216 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:53.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
But despite the shutdown,
the FDA is trying to restart

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
their inspections
of risky foods,

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:58.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
though so far
it's just one guy going,

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:00.493 line:92%
"Does this smell bad to you?

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:03.129 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Try it. Drink it."

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.264 line:92%
And the CEO of Delta said

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:07.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
the shutdown has already cost
the airline $25 million.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:10.437
He's not that worried,
because they'll make it all back

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:14.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
if two people pay
to check their bags, so...

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:16.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We're back!
-"Come on. We're back.

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:18.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We're back, baby!"
-Come on!"

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.579 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-But Trump's been upset

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
with how the media
has covered the shutdown.

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:23.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this week, he tweeted
that the fake news

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.518 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
needed to "chill."

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:27.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, well, here's what
three different news networks

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:30.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
were covering at the
exact same time this morning.

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:35.695
Let's see if any of them took
Trump's advice about chilling.

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:37.397 line:92%
-All of these tributaries

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:39.666
are going to come rolling
into the same place --

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:45.238
Russia, Mueller,
stuff we don't even know about.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The damage
being done to the economy

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:50.610 line:92%
is worse than they predicted.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:54.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you can make a snowman
feminine or masculine.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.281 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You have the ability.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But you don't want to hurt
the feelings of the snowwoman.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:59.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. I mean, you could make
a separate snowwoman.

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:00.920 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:04.057 size:78% position:39%
-Seemed pretty chill,
those last people.

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:06.326
As I mentioned, last night,
we had our Puerto Rico show,

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:08.862
but that meant we missed
something pretty incredible

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:10.029 line:92%
that happened in the news.

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:12.332
I'm talking about
President Trump buying fast food

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.900 line:92%
for the Clemson football team.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:19.672
and sending a tweet that said
he ordered "1,000 hamberders."

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:22.909 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:25.912 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hamberders.

00:02:25.912 --> 00:02:28.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hamberders sounds like
how you would say "hamburgers"

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:30.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
if your mouth
was full of hamburgers.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hamberder.
I need a hamberder."

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.687 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.456 line:92%
Later, Trump told Secret Service

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:39.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
to keep an eye out
for the Hamberdergler.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.462 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.496 line:92%
-Well, people have been saying

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:45.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Trump has been bored
during the shutdown

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:47.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
and spending a lot of time
looking out windows.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.503
You know, until one of his
staffers finally tapped him

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:54.073
on the shoulder and said,
"Sir, that's a microwave."

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:56.009 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.278 size:81% position:41% line:92%
"It's filthy outside."

00:02:58.278 --> 00:03:01.181
Trump has been complaining
about being stuck inside

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:03.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
the White House
during the shutdown.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.217 line:92%
He's actually been so bored,

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:05.785 align:start size:94% position:6%
he started writing a book
about his experience.

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:08.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think he might have been
inspired by Dr. Seuss.

00:03:08.188 --> 00:03:08.855 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Check this out.

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.924
It starts, "The sun did not
shine, I did nothing at all.

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:14.794
All alone in the White House,
cause they won't build my wall.

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:17.330 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:21.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just sat there on Twitter
refreshing fake news

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:23.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
and said how I wish
I had something to do.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:27.507
They won't give me my slats
or concrete or steel girders.

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:31.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I guess I'll stay home
and eat all the hamberders."

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:34.280 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:35.248 size:75% position:38% line:92%
He's onto something.

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:36.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow. He's onto
something, right?

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.384 line:92%
-Here's another big story.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:40.620
Confirmation hearings are
under way for Trump's pick

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:43.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
for attorney general,
William Barr.

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:43.957 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
There he is.

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:48.127
Looks like Peter Griffin from
"Family Guy" with a law degree.

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:51.531 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.531 --> 00:03:52.298 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Some entertainment news.

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:56.269
The first trailer for the new
Spider-Man movie just came out.

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:57.070 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:59.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's already causing
a lot of excitement.

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:00.473 line:92%
In this movie, Peter Parker

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:02.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
flies to Europe
for a school trip.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.177 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Check out the trailer.

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:06.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Planning a trip?
-Mm-hmm. Going to Europe.

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:08.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a school trip.
-Get your passport?

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:11.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Peter Parker here to
pick up a passport, please.

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:12.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mini toothpaste?
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:14.087 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Pack your suit.

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:18.324
-TSA security is closed
due to the government shutdown.

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:19.792 line:92%
All flights are canceled.

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.027 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-What just happened?

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:23.396 line:92%
"Spider-Man: Staying Home."

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:25.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Staying Home."
-Wow.

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:28.601 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:29.936 line:92%
-Well, here's a local story.

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:31.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yesterday the old
Tappan Zee Bridge

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:33.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
was demolished
with a controlled explosion.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a lot of people
stood around for hours

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:37.277 line:92%
to watch the big moment live.

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:38.578 line:92%
Well, it happened pretty fast.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:41.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
Listen to what one guy shouted
on TV right after.

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:44.384
-All four right here of the
shots that we have of this.

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:46.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
We got you -- Oh.
-There it goes!

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:48.388 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-There it is.

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:50.189 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, I missed it!

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:53.359 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.429 --> 00:04:57.463 line:92%
-That guy's wife was like,

00:04:57.463 --> 00:05:01.401 size:84% position:42%
"You just had to go get
a hot dog, didn't you?"

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:05.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ah. That poor guy has no luck.
I guess he's a cameraman.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.506 line:92%
Check out what happened to him

00:05:06.506 --> 00:05:08.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
when they blew up
the Georgia Dome.

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:11.210 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Really?

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.880 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Got a bus, dude!

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:14.947 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
A bus!

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:18.251 line:92%
Geez! Get out of the way, bus!

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:22.355 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:24.190 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Ugh!

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:25.692 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:28.127 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Can you imagine that?

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:28.961 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughs ]

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:31.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
And finally, listen to this.
China just made history

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:34.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
by growing the first plant
on the Moon.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.903
When asked what type of plant
it is, China's astronaut said...

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:38.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
[Inhales sharply]
"Don't worry about it."

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:42.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a great show tonight.
Give it up for The Roots!

